adr: 0363
file: lib/dialect/pasprocess.pas
kills: lib_process_execute
why: The chr(0) check in AddArg is taken out, so a word holding one reaches ADR-0122's crossing and the program stops instead of answering errSyntax. Case 17 is the word; what fails is the whole case, the process having ended there.
--- old
  else if HoldsNul(arg) then
    AddArg := errSyntax
--- new
  else if false then
    AddArg := errSyntax
